(load "Test.carp")
(load "http.carp")

(Project.config "title" "http")
(Project.config "docs-directory" "./docs/")
(Project.config "docs-logo" "")
(Project.config "docs-url" "https://github.com/carpentry-org/http")
(Project.config "docs-styling" "../style.css")
(Project.config "docs-prelude" "An HTTP request/response parser and serializer
for Carp.

Parse requests with [`Request.parse`](./Request.html#parse), responses with
[`Response.parse`](./Response.html#parse). Build requests with
[`Request.get`](./Request.html#get), [`Request.post`](./Request.html#post), etc.

Status codes are available as constants in the [`Status`](./Status.html) module.
Form bodies can be parsed with [`Form.parse`](./Form.html#parse), and
`multipart/form-data` ones with
[`Request.multipart-data`](./Request.html#multipart-data).

Content is negotiated with [`Accept`](./Accept.html),
[`AcceptEncoding`](./AcceptEncoding.html) and
[`AcceptLanguage`](./AcceptLanguage.html), or the `Request` wrappers around them.
[`Auth`](./Auth.html) reads and writes the RFC 7235 authentication headers,
[`ByteRange`](./ByteRange.html) the RFC 9110 range headers.

### Parsing
```
(match (Request.parse \"GET / HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: example.com\\r\\n\\r\\n\")
  (Result.Success req) (println* (Request.verb &req))
  (Result.Error e) (IO.errorln &e))
```

### Status codes
```
Status.ok           ; => 200
Status.not-found    ; => 404
(Status.reason 200) ; => \"OK\"
```")

(save-docs Request
           Response
           Cookie
           SameSite
           HttpDate
           Status
           Form
           Multipart
           FormPart
           TransferEncoding
           MediaType
           Accept
           MediaRange
           AcceptEncoding
           AcceptLanguage
           Weighted
           Auth
           Credentials
           ByteRange
           ByteRangeSpec
           ContentRange
           CacheControl)
(quit)
